  "findings": [
    "Plain and PCH-create objects retain an ordinary non-COMDAT 124-byte constants section before the SEH and string COMDAT contributions.",
    "PCH-use suppresses both the 124-byte constants and the 2176-byte dewindow table, along with all 32 header storage symbols. It preserves the relative order and payloads of the remaining .rdata contributions.",
    "All 35 complete emitted function bodies and their relocation target identities are unchanged in both PCH controls. This compares the controls with each other, not a claim of 35 exact original-DLL matches.",
    "The source-header-end control was already performed by the integration owner and was not repeated. The C++ suppression control is separately documented in analysis/audio-mp3-storage-audit.json."
  ],
  "conclusion": "This ordinary PCH mechanism suppresses common-header storage; it does not move copy 11 after literals. A PCH reconstruction would require independent evidence of a real creator unit and correct accounting for both repeated table families. There is no justification here to change canonical source, add a data-only unit, duplicate constants, or force section order. The original translation-unit boundary/data-order issue remains unresolved.",
  "limitations": "No whole-DLL link or new source-layout inference was established. This bounded negative control does not rule out every possible historical build mechanism.",
